{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>There is no darkening</b> — from the root of ותכהין עיניו (and his eyes dim), that it not spread; the opposite of פשה הנגע (the spread of the affliction); then it begins to heal. Some say: like חשכה (it grew dark). And the word נחלה is from the nifal binyan, from the root חלי, and the verb is past, or it is an adjective and lacks the word היא (it is), because the aged man, since the skin wrinkles around the eye — and likewise the pupil does not spread — as stated, ותכהין עיניו, and so the affliction: when it is dark, the measure of the affliction contracts and does not spread; then it begins to heal."], :book :nahum, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nahum -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nachum"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:45.392098865Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}